Z||000000||bHooper||09-29-2000||02:02 AM||||I need to "Burp" my fiero... what is the "proper" way to do this?<P>TIA!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||overlord||09-29-2000||05:28 AM||||im assuming u mean the cooling system..<BR>just did this the other day, and like u didnt know the proper procedure so i just opened up both coolant caps (at engine and rad.), took out the thermometer, heard some air hissing out, then poured coolant in the engine end until it started to come out the front end.   worked good.....cool as can be now.<P>if u do a search i imagine there is a tonne of stuff on the forum about this.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-29-2000||08:58 AM||||The easiest way is to park on an incline with the nose pointing down. Remove front radiator cap. Remove rear thermostat cap and thermostat. Fill from back. When front starts to overflow, cap front and fill back to top. With rear cap still off, start car. Level will drop slightly. Top off then install thermostat and cap. Let car warm up and make sure you have no leaks and no overheating.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||09-29-2000||06:48 AM||||thats exactly what i did... although not intentional.  i had the rear up on the jack stands so i could replace the belt, and topped off the collant that way.<P>thats a easy way... even if i didnt know it was the right way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
